# Publishable frontend configuration only. Copy to .env.local for development.
# 1. Connect an email service in the EmailJS dashboard.
# 2. Create a template: fixed To Email = anhduc.coder@gmail.com,
#    From Name = {{from_name}}, Subject = {{subject}}, Reply-To = {{reply_to}}.
#    Include {{from_name}}, {{from_email}}, {{subject}}, {{message}} in its body.
# 3. Copy the Service ID, Template ID, and Account Public Key below.
# 4. Add the production origin to EmailJS Domains; configure the same variables
#    in your hosting build environment, then rebuild/redeploy.
# Never put SMTP passwords, private API keys, or EmailJS private keys in VITE_.
# Full setup and delivery checks: docs/contact-setup.md
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=anhduc.coder@gmail.com
